github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/windows_amd64
================================================

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) built for windows_amd64 as shared libraries, so that an app
ships them and a user can replace them (LGPL 2.1 section 6b), in two codec
sets (belluikit/goffmpeg#41). An app's binary loads one of them.

shared/ holds the media set, which on desktop keeps every decoder, demuxer
and parser FFmpeg has, plus dav1d for AV1, and one input device, for
webcam capture.

  avcodec-goffmpeg-63.dll avdevice-goffmpeg-63.dll avformat-goffmpeg-63.dll avutil-goffmpeg-61.dll libavcodec-goffmpeg.dll.a libavdevice-goffmpeg.dll.a libavformat-goffmpeg.dll.a libavutil-goffmpeg.dll.a libswresample-goffmpeg.dll.a libswscale-goffmpeg.dll.a swresample-goffmpeg-7.dll swscale-goffmpeg-10.dll

shared-audio/ holds the audio set: MP3, WAV and Opus (in Ogg), with no
libswscale and no libavdevice.

  avcodec-goffmpeg-audio-63.dll avformat-goffmpeg-audio-63.dll avutil-goffmpeg-audio-61.dll libavcodec-goffmpeg-audio.dll.a libavformat-goffmpeg-audio.dll.a libavutil-goffmpeg-audio.dll.a libswresample-goffmpeg-audio.dll.a swresample-goffmpeg-audio-7.dll

lib/ contains libgoffmpeg.dll, goffmpeg's purego bridge (see Bridge below).

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
No local patches: goffmpeg's build applies patches/*.patch to the FFmpeg
checkout, and goffmpeg has no such files (BUILDING.md: "The directory is
currently empty").

License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The full
text is in LICENSE at the root of this repository, and is included in this
module's zip by the go command. The build used neither --enable-gpl nor
--enable-nonfree; each library reports "license: LGPL version 2.1 or later".

lib/libgoffmpeg.dll and the DLLs in shared/ are linked by mingw-w64 GCC (Ubuntu 24.04's mingw-w64 package) and so
contain parts of the MinGW-w64 runtime (startup code and C runtime glue).
Some of it requires its copyright and license notices to accompany
binaries: they are in COPYING.MinGW-w64-runtime.txt in this module, taken
from mingw-w64's own copy of that file.
libgcc is linked statically (-static-libgcc) and is under the GCC Runtime
Library Exception, which permits this without further notice.

